userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the shared choice-question contract and a backwards-compatible, validated session askChoices port.

**Motivation** — The native `ask_human` tool takes only `{ text }` (`packages/nax-agent/src/native/session/ask-human.ts`), so a model that wants a choice has to write the options into prose.

**Approach** — Data contract (nax-agent, exported from `.`)

New module `packages/nax-agent/src/session/choice-questions.ts`:

```ts
export interface ChoiceOption {
  readonly label: string;
  readonly description?: string;
}
export interface ChoiceQuestion {
  /** Short tab label; cut to CHOICE_HEADER_MAX_CHARS. */
  readonly header: string;
  readonly question: string;
  readonly options: readonly ChoiceOption[];
  readonly multiSelect: boolean;
  /** Whether a free-text "Other" answer is accepted. */
  readonly allowOther: boolean;
  /** Whether the person must answer it; a non-required question may be left empty. */
  readonly required: boolean;
}
export interface ChoiceAnswer {
  /** 0-based option indexes, ascending, unique. */
  readonly selected: readonly number[];
  readonly other?: string;
}
export interface ChoiceAskResult {
  /** What the person's answer reads as: formatChoiceAnswers(...) or the raw text of a plain reply. */
  readonly text: string;
  /** Absent when the embedder answered with a plain { text } reply. */
  readonly answers?: readonly ChoiceAnswer[];
}
export const CHOICE_MAX_QUESTIONS = 4;
export const CHOICE_HEADER_MAX_CHARS = 16;
export function parseChoiceQuestions(
  input: unknown,
  limits: { readonly maxOptions: number; readonly allowOther: boolean },
): { readonly ok: true; readonly questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[] } | { readonly ok: false; readonly reason: string };
export function validateChoiceAnswers(questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[], answers: unknown): string | undefined;
export function formatChoiceAnswers(questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[], answers: readonly ChoiceAnswer[]): string;
export function renderChoiceQuestionsText(prompt: string, questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[]): string;
```

- `parseChoiceQuestions` accepts an array of 1 to `CHOICE_MAX_QUESTIONS` objects, each with a non-empty string `question`, a string `header` (cut to `CHOICE_HEADER_MAX_CHARS` characters; an empty or missing header becomes `Q<n>`, 1-based), an `options` array of 2 to `limits.maxOptions` objects each with a non-empty string `label` and an optional string `description`, and an optional boolean `multiSelect` (default `false`). `allowOther` is copied from `limits.allowOther` and `required` is `true`. Option labels must be unique within one question (case-insensitive). Any other shape returns `{ ok: false, reason }`. The reason names the first failing path, for example `questions[1].options: expected 2-8 options, got 1`.
- `validateChoiceAnswers` returns `undefined` for a valid answer list and a reason string otherwise. The list is valid when all of these hold:
  - it is an array with exactly one entry per question;
  - every `selected` index is an integer in range, unique and ascending;
  - a single-select entry has at most one selected index, and never both a selected index and `other`;
  - `other` is present only when `allowOther` is true, and is then a non-empty string after trimming;
  - an entry for a `required` question has at least one selected index or an `other`.

  An entry for a non-required question may be `{ selected: [] }`.
- `formatChoiceAnswers` returns one line per question, joined with `\n`. Each line is `<question> -> <labels>`, where `<labels>` is the selected option labels in index order joined with `, `, followed by `Other: "<other>"` (joined with `, ` when labels precede it) when `other` is set. An empty non-required entry reads `(skipped)`. Example: `Which checks? -> lint, tests, Other: "e2e smoke"`.
- `renderChoiceQuestionsText` produces the plain-text rendering every consumer that ignores `questions` still shows: `prompt` (when non-empty) and then, per question, the question line (prefixed `(n/m) ` when m > 1), numbered option lines `n. label - description` (just `n. label` without a description), and the instruction line `Reply with one number or label.` (single) or `Reply with numbers or labels, separated by commas.` (multi).

Session surface (nax-agent)

Symbols the feature changes. The baseline exists only to locate the code and is never the interface to implement.

- `SessionEvent` `question` variant (`packages/nax-agent/src/session/agent-session-types.ts`). Baseline: `{ type: "question"; requestId; text; expiresAt; answerable?: false }`. Target: the same plus `readonly questions?: readonly ChoiceQuestion[]` and `readonly prompt?: string`, both set only on a choice ask. For a choice ask, `text` carries `renderChoiceQuestionsText(prompt, questions)`, so a consumer that reads only `text` (koda, the nax-agent ACP server, Telegram) still shows every option.
- `AnswerReply`. Baseline: `{ decision } | { text }`. Target: `{ readonly decision: "allow" | "deny" } | { readonly text: string; readonly answers?: readonly ChoiceAnswer[] }`.
- `SessionAskPort` (`packages/nax-agent/src/session/session-backend.ts`). Target: adds the optional method `askChoices?(prompt: string, questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[], opts?: { readonly signal?: AbortSignal }): Promise<ChoiceAskResult | null>`. It is optional so the existing nax implementer (`packages/nax/src/agents/acp/ask-port.ts`) and test fakes keep compiling.
- `PendingAskTable.issue` (`packages/nax-agent/src/session/pending-asks.ts`). Baseline: `issue(kind, signal)`. Target: `issue(kind, signal, validate?: (reply: AnswerReply) => string | undefined)`. `answer()` runs `validate` only while the entry is pending, after the kind check. When it returns a string, `answer()` throws `AgentSessionError` code `AGENT_SESSION_INVALID_ANSWER` with that string in its message and leaves the request pending.
- `createSessionAskPort` (`packages/nax-agent/src/session/session-ask-port.ts`) implements `askChoices`. It issues a `question` entry whose validator rejects an `answers` field that fails `validateChoiceAnswers`, and emits the `question` event with `questions`, `prompt` and the rendered `text`. A human settlement resolves to `{ text: formatChoiceAnswers(questions, answers), answers }` when the reply carries `answers`, and to `{ text: reply.text }` otherwise. Deadline, cancel and no running turn resolve to `null`, as `askQuestion` does today.
- `src/index.ts` is exactly 600 lines today, which is the source-file cap; `check:file-sizes` fails at 601 and nax-agent's baseline grandfathers nothing. Any story that adds names to the `.` entry has to keep the file at or under 600 lines (for example by combining re-export statements), with every export still named.

**Scope** — In: shared pure parser/validator/formatters, additive event/reply types, optional port method, pending-entry validation and session settlement, named exports and regenerated API snapshot. Out: native tool schema/routing and InteractionHandler changes (US-002), ACP form translation (US-003), reducer (US-004), chat card/controller (US-005). The nax-agent ACP server (`packages/nax-agent-acp/src/server/questions.ts`) forwards a choice ask to its ACP client as today's text question built from the event's rendered `text`; mapping `questions` to an ACP elicitation form for that client is not part of this feature. koda does not render choice questions in this feature; koda's existing `{ text }` reply to a `question` event keeps working.

**Interface** — Use the verbatim TypeScript declarations above and these target session signatures:
```ts
{ readonly decision: "allow" | "deny" } | { readonly text: string; readonly answers?: readonly ChoiceAnswer[] }
askChoices?(prompt: string, questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[], opts?: { readonly signal?: AbortSignal }): Promise<ChoiceAskResult | null>
issue(kind, signal, validate?: (reply: AnswerReply) => string | undefined)
```

Implementation/test notes: add packages/nax-agent/test/unit/session/choice-questions.test.ts; extend existing session-ask-port.test.ts and pending-asks.test.ts with controlled timers and turn signals, keeping existing assertions. Demonstrate regression tests fail on old behavior. Regenerate api/nax-agent.api.txt with `bun run api:update` in packages/nax-agent, never hand-edit it; retain every existing named export while staying within 600 lines.

**Goal** — Translate eligible ACP select-only elicitation forms into one structured ask and map its answers back to original ACP field values.

**Motivation** — `packages/nax-agent-acp/src/client/elicitation.ts` asks a form one field at a time as a text question (`questionText` renders `1. label - description` lines plus an instruction), then matches the typed reply by number, value or label (`matchChoice`).

**Approach** — ACP elicitation (nax-agent-acp)

In `packages/nax-agent-acp/src/client/elicitation.ts`, `askFields` takes a choice path when all of these hold: the context's ask port has `askChoices`; after companion folding every field is `single` or `multi`; and there are 1 to `CHOICE_MAX_QUESTIONS` fields. The path maps each field to a `ChoiceQuestion`:

- `header`: the field title or key, through `shown()`, cut to `CHOICE_HEADER_MAX_CHARS`.
- `question`: title and description joined as `questionText` joins them today, through `shown()`.
- options: the field's choices, with label and description through `shown()`.
- `multiSelect` for `multi`, and `required` from the field.
- `allowOther` when the field has a companion, except a required single-select, which gets `false`. This matches `ownAnswerHint`, which offers no own answer there today.

It makes one call, `askChoices(shown(message), questions, { signal: ctx.signal })`, wrapped in `.catch(() => null)` as `ask()` wraps `askQuestion`, and skipped with a cancel when `ctx.signal.aborted`, as `ask()` does. Any other form keeps the existing one-field-at-a-time path unchanged.

Mapping the result to elicitation content:
- `answers` present:
  - a single field takes `{ [key]: choice.value }` for its selected index;
  - a multi field takes `{ [key]: [values in index order] }`;
  - `other` takes `{ [companion]: other }`;
  - an empty entry for a non-required field sets no key.
- A required multi-select answered with only `other` declines with `REQUIRED_NOTE` noted. This matches today's rule that a companion only adds to a choice.
- `answers` absent (a plain text reply) and exactly one field: the reply goes through the existing `applyReply(field, text)`. With more than one field it declines with `NO_MATCH_NOTE` noted.
- `null` cancels, as today.

**Scope** — In: select-only choice branch in askFields, sanitized ChoiceQuestion mapping, original-value structured response mapping, plain text/null/rejection/abort behavior and ACP handler integration tests. Out: shared choice/session contract (US-001), native tool support (US-002), reducer (US-004), chat rendering/controller (US-005). The nax run-time ACP ask port (`packages/nax/src/agents/acp/ask-port.ts`), `run-interaction-handler.ts` and the Telegram/webhook interaction plugins do not implement `askChoices`; they keep the text path, which carries the rendered options. Elicitation forms that mix text fields with select fields, or carry more than four select fields, keep the existing one-field-at-a-time text path. The nax-agent ACP server (`packages/nax-agent-acp/src/server/questions.ts`) forwards a choice ask to its ACP client as today's text question built from the event's rendered `text`; mapping `questions` to an ACP elicitation form for that client is not part of this feature.

**Interface** — Consumed public contract from `@nathapp/nax-agent`:
```ts
export interface ChoiceQuestion {
  /** Short tab label; cut to CHOICE_HEADER_MAX_CHARS. */
  readonly header: string;
  readonly question: string;
  readonly options: readonly ChoiceOption[];
  readonly multiSelect: boolean;
  /** Whether a free-text "Other" answer is accepted. */
  readonly allowOther: boolean;
  /** Whether the person must answer it; a non-required question may be left empty. */
  readonly required: boolean;
}
export interface ChoiceAnswer {
  /** 0-based option indexes, ascending, unique. */
  readonly selected: readonly number[];
  readonly other?: string;
}
export interface ChoiceAskResult {
  /** What the person's answer reads as: formatChoiceAnswers(...) or the raw text of a plain reply. */
  readonly text: string;
  /** Absent when the embedder answered with a plain { text } reply. */
  readonly answers?: readonly ChoiceAnswer[];
}
askChoices?(prompt: string, questions: readonly ChoiceQuestion[], opts?: { readonly signal?: AbortSignal }): Promise<ChoiceAskResult | null>
```

Implementation/test notes: create test/unit/client/elicitation-choices.test.ts; preserve every existing elicitation.test.ts assertion and its fakes without askChoices. Its seam AC sends a select-only `elicitation/create` form to the actual exported `answerElicitation` handler with a typed fake SessionAskPort and asserts one `askChoices` call. This is the same handler backend.ts routes to in production; follow the existing elicitation.test.ts direct-handler pattern rather than requiring a new transport harness or backend changes. Never launch a real agent. Keep profile checks, companion folding, MAX_CHOICES and MAX_FORM_FIELDS as they stand. The design's `shown(...)` shorthand means the existing `shown(text, ctx.secrets)` signature for every displayed string, including message, header, question, option labels and descriptions. Construct ACP ChoiceQuestion values directly rather than using the native-input parser: ACP required/Other/options limits differ. Pass every agent-supplied display string through shown() but retain original field keys, companion keys and choice.value for the accepted ACP content. Imports from nax-agent must use only its public entry. Choice ask timeout, cancellation, turn end and rejected askChoices all map to cancel, while the no-askChoices port keeps asking individual rendered fields as before.
